## 🔄 Key Data Flows

### 1. Job Creation (Programmer → DB)
```
ProgrammerJobForm → useJobHandlers → programmerUtils (calc) 
    → jobApi.createJobs → POST /api/jobs 
    → job.validator (Zod) → job-service.createJobs 
    → prisma.$transaction → Counter (refNumber) + Job rows
    → emitJobsUpdated (Socket.IO) → All clients refresh
```

### 2. Operator Time Logging
```
OperatorJobDetail → useOperatorRunActions → employeeLogsApi 
    → POST /api/employee-logs/operator/start
    → Machine conflict check → Active log validation
    → EmployeeLog.create (status: "ACTIVE")
    → ... work happens ...
    → POST /api/employee-logs/operator/complete
    → Duration calc → Revenue rebalancing → Capture sync
    → emitJobsUpdated → Dashboard cache invalidation
```

### 3. Revenue Rebalancing (operatorShared.ts)
When operator logs are created/completed, the system automatically:
1. Fetches all completed operator logs for the job
2. Calculates each quantity's proportional revenue based on actual worked time vs. estimated time
3. Updates `EmployeeLog.metadata` with per-quantity revenue allocations
4. Syncs `JobOperatorCapture` records

### 4. QC Flow
```
Operator sends qty to QA → JobQuantityQaState = "PENDING"
QC views → Approve/Reject per quantity
Reject → Notification to operator for rework
All approved → Group qcDecision = "APPROVED"
```

### 5. Dashboard Metrics (Cached)
```
Client → GET /api/dashboard?view=programmer&preset=this_week
    → cacheGet("dashboard:programmer:...") 
    → If miss: Query Jobs + EmployeeLogs → Aggregate → cacheSet (60s TTL)
    → Return grouped metrics, activity feed, revenue charts
```

